              "node_type": "item",
              "title": "📄 StepJack: Benchmarking Computer-Use Agent Safety Against Multi-Step Indirect Prompt Injection — Zhan et al., 2026. Introduces multi-step indirect prompt injection, decomposing an adversarial goal into innocuous-looking sub-steps distributed across a chain of pages along the agent's navigation path; the resulting 480-example StepJack benchmark raises attack success on computer-use agents by up to 31.2 points at fixed decomposition depth (e.g., GPT-5.4-mini 41.7%→72.9%). Code",
              "description": ".",
